[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Its reports show three
problems. The queued parser fix closes one of them. The other two keep coming after it ships.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below now has a ticket of its own. Count reports against the ticket
for their problem, not against #4471.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} {labels} />

- **Shared parser reads month first.** Every tenant writes the day first. The parser swaps day and
  month on any date with a day of 12 or less: a booking for 7 April becomes an invite for 4 July.
  This is the bug #4471 is named for. [Ticket](https://github.com/jpalmowski/support-kb/issues/1).
- **booking-v3 hint says MM/DD.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field,
  then reads the field day first. People type what the hint says, and the date flips before it
  reaches the parser. Fixing the parser does not fix this.
  [Ticket](https://github.com/jpalmowski/support-kb/issues/2).
- **Booking moves one day.** Some reports describe a one-day shift, not a swap. The same meeting
  shows Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto, and an invite can arrive before its booking. That
  is a time-zone conversion bug. The desk noted these reports (`oneDayMove`) but filed them under
  the parser. [Ticket](https://github.com/jpalmowski/support-kb/issues/3).

## How the reports are placed

A report's problem comes from where it was made, not from its subject line or its intake tag:

1. Take each report once. The export repeats some reports across pages, so count by id.
2. Tenant and channel decide the cause (`causes.ts`): a day-first tenant using the booking-v3
   form has the hint problem. Every other report from a day-first tenant has the parser problem.
3. A report the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) has the time-zone problem,
   whatever its tenant.

The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. It disagrees with the tenant on dozens of
these reports, in both directions, so it does not decide the problem.

The kb's own cause table for #4471, for comparison. It already marks the hint problem as having
no ticket, and it counts the one-day moves under the parser:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What changes for the desk

- A date report from a booking-v3 tenant's form goes to the hint ticket, not to #4471.
- A report of a booking moved by one day goes to the time-zone ticket, not to #4471.
- Merging on subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put all three
  problems in one ticket. Before merging a date report, check the tenant, the channel and what the
  body shows.

